From: Will Deacon <willdeacon@google.com>
Date: Tue Apr 21 13:44:28 2026 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ANDROID: KVM: arm64: Handle missing userspace mapping in pKVM mem abort

When a p-guest stage-2 fault occurs, the host looks at the stage-1
mapping to check if it is backed by a single PAGE_SIZE page or a THP.

Under heavy memory pressure, that userspace mapping can be momentarily
absent which is unhandled in the abort path and will lead to a crash.

Catch this error and skip the stage-2 mapping attempt. This fault will
be retried later either on a subsequent memory access or via a new
kvm_hyp_req.

Bug: 500876966
Bug: 503427706
Change-Id: I940dc01e29454f75fe2a2766c61804ceba9e12d3
Signed-off-by: Will Deacon <willdeacon@google.com>

[gki6677 reshape note - 2026-11-02, Z.ai]
Reshaped for the 6.6.77 pin. The pin's transparent_hugepage_adjust()
returns long and propagates negative errnos from
get_user_mapping_size() when the userspace mapping is momentarily
absent (heavy memory pressure), but the pin stores the result into
an unsigned long page_size - the error wraps into a garbage huge
size and the abort path crashes (the exact scenario of Bugs
500876966/503427706). Reshape: page_size split out of the pin's
unsigned multi-declaration as long (upstream's vintage declares it
standalone), and the upstream negative check inserted right after
the adjust call. The new exit path additionally executes
mmap_read_unlock(mm) before goto unpin, because our 0046 reshape
holds the lock from pin_user_pages() through the adjustment
(upstream releases earlier, so its form needs no unlock here).
The -EAGAIN ? 0 : error form is kept verbatim from upstream. No
-EAGAIN producer exists at the pin today; the form is future-proof
and upstream-faithful. Verified: strict git apply on the pin
replica + exit-path walk.

Origin: android.googlesource.com/kernel/common 1569a00286640e452ce917ee8b3cec04c5cc3715
Batch: B-2 (P4 kvm/pKVM cluster) - Class B, RESHAPED for the pin; predicted ABI delta zero

---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/kvm/mmu.c b/arch/arm64/kvm/mmu.c
index fc4fe8a47..905f53099 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/kvm/mmu.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kvm/mmu.c
@@ -1707,7 +1707,8 @@ static int pkvm_mem_abort(struct kvm_vcpu *vcpu, phys_addr_t *fault_ipa,
 {
 	unsigned int flags = FOLL_HWPOISON | FOLL_LONGTERM | FOLL_WRITE;
 	struct kvm_hyp_memcache *hyp_memcache = &vcpu->arch.stage2_mc;
-	unsigned long index, pmd_offset, page_size, end;
+	unsigned long index, pmd_offset, end;
+	long page_size;
 	struct mm_struct *mm = current->mm;
 	struct kvm_pinned_page *ppage;
 	struct kvm *kvm = vcpu->kvm;
@@ -1766,6 +1767,14 @@ static int pkvm_mem_abort(struct kvm_vcpu *vcpu, phys_addr_t *fault_ipa,
 	page_size = transparent_hugepage_adjust(kvm, memslot,
 						hva, &pfn,
 						fault_ipa);
+
+	/* Stage-1 mapping missing. Retry the fault. */
+	if (page_size < 0) {
+		ret = page_size == -EAGAIN ? 0 : page_size;
+		mmap_read_unlock(mm);
+		goto unpin;
+	}
+
 	page = pfn_to_page(pfn);
 
 		mmap_read_unlock(mm);
